From b525086b7300262b569638193f3880c4c4a5d7d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: martinsngr <martin.sinegre@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:03:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] I: opt-in no-slip at porous/free Darcy faces

Problem. Next to a porous surface the viscous term of the free cell couples
it to the porous cell centre (distance dx instead of dx/2 for a wall) with
the viscosity interpolated between the free and the porous cell; in a dry
porous cell the mixture is air, so next to water the coefficient is about
half the water viscosity. Together: about a quarter of a wall's shear. The
free fluid nearly slips along the porous surface (slit between impermeable
porous walls, 8 cells: near-wall/mean velocity 0.78 with H and F', 0.59
with this term using the interpolated viscosity, 0.41 with real walls) and
capillary rise was 12-28 % too fast.

Change (UEqn.H, keyword porousFreeNoSlip 1 in transportProperties,
default 0 = previous behaviour): an implicit face Laplacian on porous/free
Darcy faces (DarcyFace = 1, Solidf = 0, i.e. sqrt(K) well below the cell
size) that raises the total viscous coefficient there to 2*mu_free, i.e.
shear mu_free*(U_P - U_porous)/(dx/2): no-slip relative to the porous cell
velocity at the surface (Beavers-Joseph slip ~ sqrt(K) neglected). The
added coefficient is bounded below by 0: next to a wet porous cell the
interpolated viscosity can exceed 2*mu_free of an air-filled free cell, and
reducing the coupling there gave fast air currents along wet walls (10-60
m/s, not understood); those faces keep the previous coupling. Uniform
meshes assumed (0.5 interpolation weights). momentumPredictor off in the
tested cases (the term enters through UEqn.A()/H()).

Checks (with H and F', slit 2 ms, 8-cell porous walls): impermeable porous
walls (K 1e-20) vs real walls with constantAlphaContactAngle: gap 4/8/15
cells, theta 40/60/80 deg all within 2 % (1.33/1.32, 1.27/1.25, 1.01/0.99,
1.57/1.54, 0.73/0.72 mm); yarn-like walls (K 1e-11) stable, max |U| about
1 m/s; 10 um vs 20 um mesh: 20 um 4 % fast; water budget closed to 1e-25.
Keyword off: bit-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 solvers/hybridPorousInterFoam/UEqn.H          | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../createPorousMediaFields.H                 |  7 ++++++
 2 files changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/solvers/hybridPorousInterFoam/UEqn.H b/solvers/hybridPorousInterFoam/UEqn.H
index 43ab40a..7009b08 100644
--- a/solvers/hybridPorousInterFoam/UEqn.H
+++ b/solvers/hybridPorousInterFoam/UEqn.H
@@ -11,6 +11,31 @@
 	//Implicit Drag Term
         + fvm::Sp(Drag,U)
 
+        // Change I (opt-in porousFreeNoSlip 1): no-slip at the porous
+        // surface. On porous/free Darcy faces (sqrt(K) << cell size) the
+        // viscous term above couples the free cell to the porous cell centre
+        // (distance dx) with the viscosity interpolated between the free and
+        // the porous cell (air in a dry yarn: about half the water viscosity
+        // next to water). This face term raises the coefficient to
+        // 2*mu_free: shear mu_free*(U_P - U_porous)/(dx/2), i.e. the velocity
+        // of the porous cell at the surface, as a wall (Beavers-Joseph slip
+        // ~ sqrt(K) neglected). Uniform meshes (linear weights 0.5).
+        // Never below the interpolated coupling: air next to a wet porous
+        // cell keeps the (too large) interpolated viscosity; reducing it to
+        // 2*mu_air gave fast air currents along wet walls (10-60 m/s, not
+        // understood).
+      - (1./eps)*fvm::laplacian
+        (
+            porousFreeNoSlip*DarcyFace*(1. - Solidf)
+           *max
+            (
+                4.*fvc::interpolate(mixture.mu()*(1. - Solid))
+              - fvc::interpolate(mixture.mu()),
+                dimensionedScalar(dimDynamicViscosity, 0)
+            ),
+            U
+        )
+
      ==
         fvModels.source(rho, U)
     );
diff --git a/solvers/hybridPorousInterFoam/createPorousMediaFields.H b/solvers/hybridPorousInterFoam/createPorousMediaFields.H
index 244f2b7..5cded23 100644
--- a/solvers/hybridPorousInterFoam/createPorousMediaFields.H
+++ b/solvers/hybridPorousInterFoam/createPorousMediaFields.H
@@ -107,6 +107,13 @@ const scalar porousFreeFluxForce
     transportProperties.lookupOrDefault<scalar>("porousFreeFluxForce", 0)
 );
 
+// Change I (UEqn.H): no-slip at porous/free Darcy faces. 1 = on, 0 (default)
+// = viscous coupling to the porous cell centre as before.
+const scalar porousFreeNoSlip
+(
+    transportProperties.lookupOrDefault<scalar>("porousFreeNoSlip", 0)
+);
+
 // Change G (opt-in): porous/free faces carry the porous two-phase fluxes,
 // with pc = 0 in free cells and the harmonic face permeability (see
 // porousFace.H). Without the keyword porousFace = Solidf: solver unchanged.
